<title>USA: Westmoreland seeks to pay worker comp claims.</title>
<headline>Westmoreland seeks to pay worker comp claims.</headline>
<dateline>COLORADO SPRINGS, Colo. 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Westmoreland Coal Co said on Wednesday that it has submitted to the Court in its Chapter 11 bankruptcy proceeding a motion to permit the payment of workers' compensation claims.</p>
<p>The company is seeking to pay the claims from $9.7 million in cash it had posted in 1993 to collateralize its workers' compensation bonds.</p>
<p>If approved, the cash collateral will be used to reimburse state commissions and to cover payments for about 18 more months.</p>
<p>The cost of current claims are about $379,000 per month in Virginia and $36,000 per month in West Virginia.</p>
</text>
